**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests`

**How to implement.** A fit runs off the UI thread on `JobRunner` with per-iteration progress and Cancel, and its fit run is written on completion only (001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`, with progress and cancel; the fit run is written on completion'; 001 §P `RunFit`; the S11.3 brief; .spec-md §10.2 'one fit iteration … Each shows a progress bar with Cancel, through JobRunner', §10.3 'Fits … are one click with Cancel', §10.4 'The job's completion message updates the Elmish model, so the fit-run history … re-render[s] without a manual reload'). It hosts the fit as step 200 hosts an archive job, over `JobRunner.fs:startBackground`, `:updateJob` and `:JobModel`; the study view that sends `RunFit` and binds this state is S11.5's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `StudyEngine.fs`: `StudyFitError` gains `FitRunKitErr of error : KitError` (`the kit refused the fit run: <the error's describe>`) and `FitRunRaisedErr of reason : string` (`the fit raised: <reason>`). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob`, compiled directly after `KitArchiveJob.fs` (step 200), before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`, no comment. In order: (a) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitJobHandle = { cancelStudyFit : unit -> unit }`. (b) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitJobHost = { startStudyFit : (IterationWatch -> Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>) -> StudyFitJobHandle }`, with `static member posting (post : (unit -> unit) -> unit) (progressed : JobProgress -> unit) (ended : Result<FitRun, StudyFitError> -> unit) : StudyFitJobHost`: a `CancellationTokenSource` and a `Stopwatch` per job; the fit runs through `JobRunner.startBackground` as `RanToCompletion [ fit (WatchedIterations o) ]`, `o` reporting each iteration count k as `post (fun () -> progressed { completed = JobStepCount k.value; total = None; elapsed = JobElapsed <the stopwatch's elapsed> })` (an iteration count with no known total, `JobRunner.fs:JobProgress`, which `progressText` shows as `<k> iterations (<t> s)…`) over the source's token; its `onDone` posts `ended` of the fit's result, a raise (`Error (JobRunExn e)`) ending as `Error (FitRunRaisedErr e.Message)` and an outcome holding no result as `Error (FitRunRaisedErr <a reason naming it>)`; the handle cancels the source. `static member onUiThread (progressed) (ended) : StudyFitJobHost` is `posting` through Avalonia's `Dispatcher.UIThread.Post`, the host a window composes. (c) `StudyFitJobState = { job : JobModel<FitRunName>; handleOpt : StudyFitJobHandle option; errorOpt : StudyFitError option }` with `static member idle` (`initModel`, no handle, no error): the one fit a surface runs, whose committed result is the last fit run written. (d) `StudyFitMsg` = `RunFit of request : StudyFitRequest` (the semantic message the Run joint / Run stage buttons and the tests send, 001 §P) | `CancelStudyFit` | `StudyFitProgressed of progress : JobProgress` | `StudyFitEnded of result : Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>`, each case documented. (e) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitEnvironment = { host : StudyFitJobHost; fitWith : StudyFitRequest -> IterationWatch -> Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>; kit : KitProxy }`, with `static member create (host : StudyFitJobHost) (kit : KitProxy) (forward : StudyForwardContext) (clock : ClockProvider) : StudyFitEnvironment`, whose `fitWith request watch` reads `kit.readFitRuns request.study` (step 384, an error `FitRunKitErr`) and answers `{ forward; clock; linearSolver = createMathNetSvd (); deviates = UniformDeviateProvider.fromSeed (NoiseSeed 1); fitRuns }.runFit request watch` (step 391): one fixed seed, so a study refits reproducibly and every run records its starts (step 383). (f) `type StudyFitMsg with member this.updateWith (environment : StudyFitEnvironment) (state : StudyFitJobState) : StudyFitJobState`: `RunFit r` while `state.job.isRunning` changes nothing (one fit at a time), and otherwise starts `environment.fitWith r` through `environment.host.startStudyFit`, the job through `updateJob StartRequested`, holding the handle and clearing the error; `CancelStudyFit` calls the handle's `cancelStudyFit` while the job runs and changes nothing else; `StudyFitProgressed p` is `updateJob (ProgressReported p)`; `StudyFitEnded (Ok run)` writes `environment.kit.writeFitRun run` (step 384), then `updateJob (RunCompleted run.name)` with no handle and no error, or, when the kit refuses (an existing name is `FitRunExistsErr`, a read-only kit `KitReadOnlyErr`), returns the job to `Idle` with its committed result kept and holds `FitRunKitErr`; `StudyFitEnded (Error (FitCancelledErr _))` is `updateJob RunCancelled` with no handle, nothing written; any other error returns the job to `Idle`, its committed result kept, and holds the error. This is the only place a fit run is written. No queue, retry, second job or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs`, `module StudyFitJobTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over `KitProxy.createInMemory` of an initialised `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 125), a host `posting` whose `post` calls at once and whose `progressed` and `ended` feed `StudyFitProgressed` and `StudyFitEnded` back through `updateWith`, test-local `fitWith` stubs answering step 384's test-local fit run, and waits on a `ManualResetEventSlim` with a ten-second limit, never a sleep: `RunFit reports each iteration, then writes the fit run once the fit completes`: a stub reporting iterations 1, 2 and 3 through its watch then answering the run leaves the state `Completed` with that name committed, its last progress `completed` 3 with no total and a progress text starting `3 iterations`, and `readFitRuns` answering the run; `a cancelled fit writes nothing and keeps the last committed fit run`: after a completed first run, a stub that waits until its watch's cancellation is requested and answers `FitCancelledErr`, sent `CancelStudyFit`, leaves the state `Cancelled` with the first name still committed and one fit-run file; `a fit run that would overwrite an existing one is refused and nothing is written`: with the run's name already written, the end holds `FitRunKitErr (FitRunExistsErr _)`, the job `Idle`, and the file's bytes are unchanged; `a fit that raises ends with FitRunRaisedErr carrying its message`: a stub raising `InvalidOperationException "solver gone"` ends with `FitRunRaisedErr` whose reason holds `solver gone`; `RunFit while a fit runs starts nothing`: a second `RunFit` while the first stub waits starts no second fit (the stub is called once). `StudyEngineTests`' `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.

**Acceptance.** After the job lands, `RunFit` MUST run the fit off the UI thread through `JobRunner.startBackground` with per-iteration progress and Cancel, and `StudyFitEnded` MUST write the fit run once on completion and nothing on cancel or error; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RunFit reports each iteration, then writes the fit run once the fit completes`, `a cancelled fit writes nothing and keeps the last committed fit run`, `a fit run that would overwrite an existing one is refused and nothing is written`, `a fit that raises ends with FitRunRaisedErr carrying its message` and `RunFit while a fit runs starts nothing`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.
